<title>ARGENTINA: Weather said good for Argentine crops.</title>
<headline>Weather said good for Argentine crops.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, mainly dry weather in Argentine crop zones Monday was benefitting most developing soybean, maize and sunflower crops, traders said.</p>
<p>Prospects for the maize were improved over the weekend by rain in parts of southern Buenos Aires province, although there are still plots of maize which could do with more moisture, they said.</p>
<p>The government's Meteorological Service forecast warm, humid weather. Weather Services Corp said highs would range from 84-96 F (29-36 C).</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
